       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Typical dosing is:\n\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg once daily. Use 2.5 mg for frail or elderly patients, or for patients with hepatic impairment.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg once daily.\n\nA dose of 30 mg raises the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nPlease check whether this was a typo or a mix-up with another drug or formulation. If you meant 5 mg or 10 mg, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If 30 mg is intentional, please confirm with your supervising resident or attending and with pharmacy first. I can enter it with a note once that's done."
