     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter 30 mg yet. You confirmed the dose, but you haven't told me that your attending or pharmacy has reviewed it. That was the check I asked for. This dose is three times the labeled maximum, and I can't see a clinical reason for it. A wrong order here could cause serious harm, and an order from a student is unlikely to be the right place to catch it.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose, and I can enter it now.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the standard starting dose.\n- **Enter 30 mg after your attending or pharmacist confirms it.** Tell me who approved it, and I'll enter it with a note such as \"Dose above max labeled; confirmed by Dr. X / pharmacy.\" That way the order carries the verification with it.\n\nTell me which you'd like. If the aim is better blood pressure control, your team may prefer adding a second agent to pushing amlodipine past 10 mg. That's worth raising on rounds."
      }
     ],
